<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arlanzón</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arlanzón River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arlanzón is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>. It rises in the Sierra de la Demanda and flows west through the city of Burgos before joining the Arlanza, which in turn flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisuerga">Pisuerga</a>, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Duero</a>. In antiquity its upper valley lay in the lands of the Turmodigi, and the medieval city of Burgos grew up on its banks.</p></div>
